    "description": "Third Coast Infrastructure owns and operates offshore-focused midstream assets serving Gulf of Mexico oil and natural gas production. Its customers are upstream producers that require gathering, transportation, processing, and related infrastructure services to move hydrocarbons to market. The operating model is asset-heavy and fee-based, built around pipelines, processing assets, and floating production infrastructure rather than an asset-light services platform. Public materials describe operations concentrated along the Gulf Coast and in deepwater Gulf of Mexico producing regions, including natural gas and crude pipelines, gas processing assets, NGL infrastructure, and a floating production system. Reviewed public materials indicate that J.P. Morgan Asset Management's infrastructure team has investment responsibilities for Third Coast, while the precise current ownership percentage was not publicly disclosed in the reviewed sources.",
